menu "esp-liboqs test app"

    config LIBOQS_TEST_TASK_STACK_SIZE
        int "Unity test task stack size (bytes)"
        default 24576
        help
            Stack for the FreeRTOS task that runs the Unity menu and test cases.
            With heap-backed ML-DSA/ML-KEM temporaries a few KB suffices; the
            stack_only build variant raises this to ~110 KB because ML-DSA-65
            then keeps ~56 KB of scratch on the stack.

    config LIBOQS_TEST_RUN_ALL_ON_BOOT
        bool "Run all Unity test cases automatically on boot"
        default n
        help
            When y, app_main runs every registered Unity test case once, then
            prints a completion marker — no interactive serial menu. This is the
            mode CI uses under esp-emu (ci/emu_run.py is read-only and cannot
            drive the menu). When n (default), the app presents the usual
            interactive unity_run_menu() for `idf.py monitor` and for
            pytest-embedded's run_all_single_board_cases().

endmenu
